 "nodes": [
  {
   "id": "root",
   "x": 417,
   "y": 10,
   "w": 760,
   "kind": "dark",
   "title": "Gut too SLOW, or too FAST? Which drug, and what rules it out?",
   "lines": [
    "a prokinetic must COORDINATE motility: simply boosting acetylcholine only gives uncoordinated contraction",
    "diarrhea: treat the CAUSE (pathogen, inflammation) and prevent DEHYDRATION first"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_pro",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 138,
   "w": 732,
   "h": 78,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "TOO SLOW: PROKINETICS",
   "lines": [
    "gastroparesis, constipation, some nausea and vomiting",
    "NEVER with a GI bleed, bowel obstruction or perforation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_anti",
   "x": 817,
   "y": 138,
   "w": 732,
   "h": 78,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "TOO FAST: ANTIDIARRHEALS",
   "lines": [
    "slow the gut, or cut secretion",
    "irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) with diarrhea: alosetron, a 5-HT3 ANTAGONIST, slows it"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "d2_head_0_0",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 296,
   "w": 236,
   "h": 78,
